q('3(b)',4.5,'Number Theory',r'Prove that there are $2021$ distinct positive integers whose squares all have the same decimal digits with the same multiplicities, possibly in different orders.','A sparse decimal construction keeps every square carry-free while preserving its total length; the zero multiplicity must also be checked.',['Digits & bases','Algorithms & constructions'],r'''For $k=0,1,\ldots,2020$, let $a_k=10^{2021}+10^k$. These are distinct and
$$a_k^2=10^{4042}+2\cdot10^{2021+k}+10^{2k}.$$
The three exponents are distinct, so there is no carrying. Each square has $4043$ digits: two ones, one two, and $4040$ zeros. This is the required family.''')
q('4(a)',4.5,'Geometry',r'A tetrahedron $ABCD$ satisfies $\angle BAC=\angle CAD=\angle DAB=90^\circ$. Prove $[BAC]^2+[CAD]^2+[DAB]^2=[BCD]^2$, where brackets denote triangle area.','The spatial analogue of Pythagoras can be proved by projection and similarity or by three-dimensional coordinates; the main step connects the sloping face to the three perpendicular faces.',['Solid geometry','Area & dissection','Coordinates & vectors'])
q('4(b)',4.5,'Geometry',r'The tangent at $C$ to the circumcircle of triangle $ABC$ meets line $AB$ at $D$. Distinct points $E,F$ on line $BC$ satisfy $BE=BF=|CD^2-BD^2|/BC$. Prove that $ED=CD$ or $FD=CD$.','An auxiliary circle centred at D makes the stated length a power-of-a-point expression; a directed-coordinate treatment also covers tangency.',['Circles & tangency','Power of a point','Coordinates & vectors'],r'''Put signed coordinate $t$ on line $BC$, with $B$ at $0$ and $C$ at $c=BC>0$. The equation for a point of this line to lie on the circle centred at $D$ with radius $DC$ is a monic quadratic in $t$. Its constant term is $BD^2-CD^2$, and one root is $c$. Hence its other root is
$$t_0=\frac{BD^2-CD^2}{c}.$$
The coordinates of $E,F$ are the two opposite numbers of absolute value $|t_0|$. Therefore one of them has coordinate $t_0$ and lies on that circle, as required. The argument also applies if the two circle intersections coincide.''')
